    {
      "Title": "La costa al desierto",
      "Summary": "My first view of Spain came with blue skies and sunshine as we headed down the Pyrenees into Catalunya. Just hours after being wrapped up warm for the cold and cloud of Andorra la Vella we were sitting in the sun at a caf\u00e9 in Montserrat, and the next day lying on the beach in Badalona. In six weeks we experienced the cities of Valencia, Murcia, Alicante and Almeria, besides many smaller towns; we drank wine and beer, and ate churros, in local caf\u00e9s; we experienced wild smimming in thermally heated rivers and pools; we saw forrests, mountains, beaches and deserts; we played cowboys in Texas Hollywood, Tabernas; and we had Christmas on a secluded beach near Nerja where we were able to lie in the sun and swim in the sea. What an introduction to the country!",
      "Chapter": 3,
      "StartDate": "2019-11-08",
      "EndDate": "2019-12-28",
      "Photos": [
        {
          "Chapter": 3,
          "Photo": 1,
          "Title": "Monistrol de Montserrat",
          "Summary": "Our first stop in Spain, beautiful blue skies, beautiful mountains: a great introduction. We tried ordering in Spanish for the first time: \"Un caf\u00e9 por favor\" and got back: \"Speak Catalan or English, we don't speak Spanish here\", so we were also introduced to the politics!",
          "FileName": "03-01-montserrat.jpg",
          "FileSize": 502653,
          "OriginalSize": 1497783,
          "Latitude": 41.6030806,
          "Longitude": 1.8318,
          "AspectRatio": 1.0,
          "DateTime": "2019:11:09 08:42:38"
        },
        {
          "Chapter": 3,
          "Photo": 2,
          "Title": "Beach at Badalona",
          "Summary": "Finally made it to the Mediterranean Coast, albeit a fairly industrial stretch. We just stopped here a few hours to sit on the beach before heading off: since that time we've been to hundreds of hugely varied beaches along the Spanish south coast but the sight of the sea after weeks inland is always magical.",
          "FileName": "03-02-badalona.jpg",
          "FileSize": 496573,
          "OriginalSize": 1209488,
          "Latitude": 41.4311944,
          "Longitude": 2.2395444,
          "AspectRatio": 1.0,
          "DateTime": "2019:11:09 12:09:09"
        },
        {
          "Chapter": 3,
          "Photo": 3,
          "Title": "People Towers at Granollers",
          "Summary": "This Catalonian tradition was our first taste of the spectacular and often dangerous world of Fiesta. Coming from England \u2014where we do trick-or-treat, maybe put out some decorations at Christmas and occasionally hang some bunting round the streets for Gay Pride or a royal jubilee\u2014 Spanish Fiesta can be overwhelming. They're regular, intense and often crazy. Building ten-person tall human towers with no safety net and a small child balancing on top is definitely one of the wildest!",
          "FileName": "03-03-granollers.jpg",
          "FileSize": 482090,
          "OriginalSize": 1166377,
          "Latitude": 41.6032056,
          "Longitude": 2.2877944,
          "AspectRatio": 1.0,
          "DateTime": "2019:11:09 16:57:58"
